WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.550
In 2007, just 3.4 per cent of Great
Britain's retail sales happened online.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.090
By 2019 it was 19.2 per cent.

3
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:16.710
In January 2021, during the
pandemic, it peaked at 37.8 per cent.

4
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:23.610
In 2025 it was 27.5 per cent:
about one pound in every four.

5
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.250
That brings empty units to high
streets, and more delivery vans.

6
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.550
So if you can buy almost
anything from your sofa,

7
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.630
what is the high street for?

8
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.950
In this mission, you'll weigh the costs
and benefits of shopping online and out

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.090
of town.

10
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.350
Then you'll follow London's main
shopping street as it plans its future.

11
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.800
Your mission: decide what a high
street is for in an online age.
